DD-L004 (https://driverdesk.dev/errors/DD-L004)

  × argument `speed` of `set_led` is written to the device but has no bounds
    ╭─[26-L004-unbounded-argument.yaml:38:7]
 37 │       level:   { type: u8, unit: "%" }
 38 │       speed:   { type: u16 }
    ·       ──┬──
    ·         ╰── unbounded
 39 │     send:   { header: 0x20, payload: [ { enabled: bool }, { level: u8 } ] }
    ╰────
  help: add `min`/`max` or `enum` to the argument, or a limit `safety.limits.set_led.speed` (spec
        §9.2, §14.2)
DD-L016 (https://driverdesk.dev/errors/DD-L016)

  ⚠ safety block is not signed
    ╭─[26-L004-unbounded-argument.yaml:42:1]
 41 │     timeout_ms: 50
 42 │ safety:
    · ───┬──
    ·    ╰── unsigned
 43 │   limits:
    ╰────
  help: fine for local development; the registry refuses to publish vendor descriptions with an
        unsigned safety block (spec §14.6)
